{
  "expectation_set": "tool-cases-v1",
  "adr": "0009",
  "rule": "Complete behavioral matrix for every advertised MCP tool (plan M5). Each case runs against a fresh real data root over BOTH real transports (HTTP POST /mcp and the hiero mcp stdio adapter); setup entries are complete operations (real tool calls, deterministic SQL seeds where no tool surface exists, fixture file writes), never canned responses. Persisted mutations are asserted through an independent read-only SQLite connection. Ids are pinned because a fresh database numbers series, sessions, memories, crystals, concepts, facets, and term_rules rows from 1. A string value of '*' in expected_subset matches any value (dynamic ids such as recall_id). '<ROOT>' in a string substitutes the case's data root; a string equal to '$name' substitutes a binding saved from a prior setup call's structuredContent.",
